  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Complete small early mammal with compact trunk and robust scratch-digging forelimbs; not isolated claws or skeleton. [\"LACM 150948 comprises jaws, incomplete cranium and about 40 percent of the postcranial skeleton. It is not a complete preserved skeleton.\", \"Full outline, ears, fur, tail completion and coloration are reconstructed; they must not be presented as preserved soft tissue.\", \"Basal mammalian placement is not resolved here. Do not label this animal an armadillo, anteater or confirmed placental.\", \"Scratch-digging and specialized feeding interpretations are supported by limb and tooth anatomy; exact diet remains interpretive. No detailed exposed dentition is required.\", \"Total length of approximately 16 cm is a published skeletal reconstruction estimate, not a measured holotype body length.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"total_reconstructed_length_m\": 0.16, \"head_body_length_m\": 0.1, \"tail_length_m\": 0.06, \"body_height_m\": 0.04, \"status\": \"The approximately 16 cm total length comes from Scott Hartman's author reconstruction with a 2 cm scale. Head-body, tail and height targets are approximate silhouette-derived design dimensions, not measurements of a complete fossil.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Complete small early mammal with compact trunk and robust scratch-digging forelimbs; not isolated claws or skeleton. [\"LACM 150948 comprises jaws, incomplete cranium and about 40 percent of the postcranial skeleton. It is not a complete preserved skeleton.\", \"Full outline, ears, fur, tail completion and coloration are reconstructed; they must not be presented as preserved soft tissue.\", \"Basal mammalian placement is not resolved here. Do not label this animal an armadillo, anteater or confirmed placental.\", \"Scratch-digging and specialized feeding interpretations are supported by limb and tooth anatomy; exact diet remains interpretive. No detailed exposed dentition is required.\", \"Total length of approximately 16 cm is a published skeletal reconstruction estimate, not a measured holotype body length.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"total_reconstructed_length_m\": 0.16, \"head_body_length_m\": 0.1, \"tail_length_m\": 0.06, \"body_height_m\": 0.04, \"status\": \"The approximately 16 cm total length comes from Scott Hartman's author reconstruction with a 2 cm scale. Head-body, tail and height targets are approximate silhouette-derived design dimensions, not measurements of a complete fossil.\"}"
  },
